/* =====================================================================
   PATCH 036 — connected-accounts (Google / Yahoo / Amazon linking)
   Date: 2026-10-18 | For: Jeff (Fire Babys)
   Directive: Jeff 2026-10-17 (player rebuild Part D, client half) —
     extend the profile hub's LINKED ACCOUNTS card (patch 029) with
     three more REAL OAuth providers: Google (Gmail), Yahoo, Amazon.
   What it changes:
     - Chains window.__FBPROFILE_EXT.renderInto (015 calls it, 029
       renders the hub cards, 033 chains its card) exactly like patch
       033: the previous renderer runs first, unchanged, then three
       provider rows are inserted into 029's LINKED ACCOUNTS card
       (just above the display-only handle rows). It ALSO wraps
       patch 029's own LK.renderInto (via __FBLINKS_DEBUG.store) so
       029's server-refresh re-render keeps the rows. If 029's card
       is ever absent, the rows render in their own fallback card.
     - OAuth2 flow mirrors 029's Discord flow shape-for-shape: the
       client builds the provider authorize URL (client_id comes from
       the Worker's /link/config, never hard-coded), generates state,
       stores pending+state in sessionStorage, verifies state on
       return BEFORE exchanging, and the code is exchanged
       SERVER-side via /link/<provider>/exchange — the browser's
       word alone never links anything.
