       fb_links_v1 store (acct.extLinks) for display, sanitized and
       length-capped; the Worker state always wins on refresh.
   GRACEFUL DEGRADATION (the live Worker 404s /link/* today): if
     /link/config fails or a provider is unconfigured, its row still
     renders with a VISIBLE but disabled Connect button and the
     honest note "Linking turns on soon" — no thrown errors, no
     broken card, and 029's Steam/Discord/Google-gate rows are
     untouched.
   SECURITY RULES (029's, unchanged):
     - NEVER a password field for any platform. Ever.
     - All player/provider text renders via textContent only.
     - Link changes require a live FireBabysAuth session and reuse
       029's client-side change throttle when it is available.
   Touches: DOM inside #profileOv only (rows in 029's links card).
     No canvas game code, no combat, no baseline changes.
   How to disable: set "enabled": false in patches/manifest.json, rebuild.
   Test: open the profile — LINKED ACCOUNTS shows Google (Gmail),
     Yahoo and Amazon rows; with the Worker not yet serving /link/*,
     all three show "Linking turns on soon" with disabled Connect
     buttons and zero page errors.
   ===================================================================== */
(function(){
'use strict';

var EP = {};
EP.PROVIDERS = [
  { key:'google', icon:'✉️', title:'Google (Gmail)',
    authBase:'https://accounts.google.com/o/oauth2/v2/auth',
    scope:'openid email profile', clientIdField:'googleClientId' },
  { key:'yahoo', icon:'🟪', title:'Yahoo',
    authBase:'https://api.login.yahoo.com/oauth2/request_auth',
    scope:'openid email profile', clientIdField:'yahooClientId' },
